                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da1651c9-84e5-3718-a372-b683ea8fddf8",
                        "entry_id": "7885bc11-ced8-3fdc-b424-4e54e74272b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Étape de l'histogenèse, qui voit la transformation du blastocyste en gastrula avec formation, par migration cellulaire, des tissus fondamentaux de l'embryon : les feuillets embryonnaires (le mésoblaste, l'endoblaste et l'ectoblaste)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ae1bf0d-daba-405d-8fa8-bdef7d634b96",
                                "sense_id": "da1651c9-84e5-3718-a372-b683ea8fddf8",
                                "text": "Chez l'oursin, lors de la gastrulation, va s'amorcer au pôle végétatif une invagination vers l'intérieur de ces cellules. D'autres cellules situées prés de cette plaque vont se détacher de la paroi de la blastula et devenir des cellules migratrices appelées cellules mésenchymateuses qui pénétreront dans le blastocœle."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6a7cea81-cbd6-47bd-9526-e19b7823ee3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7885bc11-ced8-3fdc-b424-4e54e74272b3",
                        "source_sense_id": "da1651c9-84e5-3718-a372-b683ea8fddf8",
                        "source_sense_description": "Sens 1",
                        "target_lang_word": "gastrulation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gastrulation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3f34ebb-6f9a-352d-b658-75dbc3ff4fdc",
                                        "entry_id": "14af2b0b-a76c-361e-80ce-76c1ca5320b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stage of embryo development at which a gastrula is formed from the blastula by the inward migration of cells."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62cdc94f-0301-4b47-bce3-ff260f7a1081",
                                                "sense_id": "f3f34ebb-6f9a-352d-b658-75dbc3ff4fdc",
                                                "text": "The study of comparative embryology, nevertheless, would lead us to expect to find this germ layer arising by a process of gastrulation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e1c71d6-18ed-4131-97a9-3727a9e0731f",
                                                "sense_id": "f3f34ebb-6f9a-352d-b658-75dbc3ff4fdc",
                                                "text": "1929, Proceedings of the South Dakota Academy of Sciences, Volumes 13-19, South Dakota Academy of Science, page 52,\nIn the instances described by various observers and in the quadruple one described herein, these gastrulations no doubt began at different times, since the embryos are of different sizes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "519798a6-d49a-4914-8138-12f8fc279993",
                                                "sense_id": "f3f34ebb-6f9a-352d-b658-75dbc3ff4fdc",
                                                "text": "2020, Konner M. Winkley, et al., 8: Tunicate Gastrulation, Lilianna Solnica-Krezel (editor), Gastrulation, Elsevier (Academic Press), page 227,\nPharmacological inhibition of RhoA at later steps of gastrulation causes the apical constrictions to relax, indicating a persistent requirement for this pathway."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
